<https://bob.example.org/2026/10/home-server-cache/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> <https://bob.example.org> .
<https://bob.example.org/2026/10/home-server-cache/> <http://purl.org/rss/1.0/title> "My home server caches everything now" .
<https://bob.example.org/2026/10/home-server-cache/> <http://purl.org/rss/1.0/link> "https://bob.example.org/2026/10/home-server-cache/" .
<https://bob.example.org/2026/10/home-server-cache/> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "https://bob.example.org/?p=412" .
<https://bob.example.org/2026/10/home-server-cache/> <http://purl.org/rss/1.0/description> "A reverse proxy, a cache, and a lot of patience. [&#8230;]" .
<https://bob.example.org/2026/10/home-server-cache/> <http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/encoded> "<p>I put a reverse proxy in front of everything. The cache hit rate is the only number I check now.</p>\n<p>The trick was honoring <code>Cache-Control</code> instead of guessing.</p>" .
